 options","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-user-interface/service-portal/c_ConfigureWidgetInstances.md","line":122},{"title":"filters","target":"c_Filters","line":131},{"title":"configuring the widget instance options","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-user-interface/service-portal/c_ConfigureWidgetInstances.md","line":207},{"title":"Configure","target":"configure-onboarding-modals","line":211},{"title":"Reference","target":"onboarding-modals-reference","line":212},{"title":"Service Portal","target":"c_ServicePortal","line":213},{"title":"Filters","target":"c_Filters","line":214},{"title":"Widget Options","target":"widget_options","line":215}],"metadata":{"title":"Widget option schema","description":"Widget instances allow users to uniquely configure each widget they add to a page. Use the option schema to define the parameters for your widget.Widget instances allow users to uniquely configure each widget they add to a page. Edit the option schema to define basic parameters for your widget.Create a table to store widget instance options instead of editing the existing option schema. When using a table as your widget option schema, you can define custom fields using any ServiceNow field type, add filters to fields, and search or query instance options.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/platform-user-interface/service-portal/c\\_WidgetInstanceOptions.html","release":"australia","product":"Service Portal","classification":"service-portal","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-04-28","reading_time_minutes":5,"breadcrumb":["Developing custom widgets","Service Portal","Configure UIs and portals","Configure user experiences"],"tags":["#platform-user-interface","#service-portal","#widgets","#themes","#self-service","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[53,59],[63,67],[73,78]],"ke